02:42.140 --> 02:47.140
<b>Two Pairs</b>

02:47.430 --> 02:49.020
I heard they're playing against Akadama.

02:49.020 --> 02:49.810
Can they win?

02:49.810 --> 02:51.150
Good luck!

02:51.150 --> 02:54.110
First set.

02:54.610 --> 02:57.320
Service side: Amamiya and Kiba pair.

02:58.070 --> 03:00.950
Receive side: Harukaze and Sawanatsu pair.

03:01.320 --> 03:02.530
Five game match.

03:02.530 --> 03:03.450
Play ball!

03:05.080 --> 03:08.200
<i>Able to win a tournament?</i>

03:08.200 --> 03:11.210
<i>They're really underestimating us.</i>

03:12.380 --> 03:15.920
<i>A simple curve ball, little speed... If it's like this...</i>

03:17.340 --> 03:18.630
<i>Flying outwards?!</i>

03:20.260 --> 03:26.100
That's something our first years can do before
even joining the Akadama Middle Soft Tennis Club.

03:27.600 --> 03:31.230
Nice receive, but a so-so return.

03:31.230 --> 03:32.560
How about this?

03:34.690 --> 03:36.440
It completely changed direction?!

03:37.530 --> 03:41.700
<i>It's a tough angle, but I can still make it in time.</i>

03:44.320 --> 03:48.790
Naive! Just hitting it isn't enough!

04:01.510 --> 04:05.590
It feels like the opponent could easily score.

04:05.590 --> 04:10.140
Just like... like a red dragonfly
hovering, waiting for its next meal.

04:10.140 --> 04:12.060
Don't describe it like that.

04:12.060 --> 04:14.560
I can't help but picture it now.

04:15.100 --> 04:17.230
Ne-Never mind.

04:17.860 --> 04:21.320
Although, this is really an exemplary game tactic.

04:22.400 --> 04:26.240
Using a slice serve to bring Asuna to the outer edge,

04:26.240 --> 04:29.200
then return the ball to the other end of the court.

04:29.200 --> 04:32.660
Even if caught in time, the well-prepared forward will smash.

04:35.500 --> 04:39.750
Those are skills expected from a regular in the regionals.

04:40.630 --> 04:41.340
But...

04:42.300 --> 04:43.380
One-Zero.

04:44.260 --> 04:47.140
Well, our attacks will only get stronger!

04:56.190 --> 04:59.190
I don't care about some ex-champion coach,

04:59.610 --> 05:01.690
'cause it looks like he can't see right.

05:04.700 --> 05:08.910
If you want to play against us,
first practice for two more years.

05:16.670 --> 05:21.710
So, the game counter stands at two-zero,

05:21.710 --> 05:24.420
only one round away from a straight set.

05:24.880 --> 05:27.050
That'll be an interesting motivator.

05:29.300 --> 05:29.970
Asuna.

05:29.970 --> 05:30.890
Y-Yes!

05:31.260 --> 05:33.220
Show off your legs more.

05:33.220 --> 05:35.980
Why'd you run long distances every day?

05:35.980 --> 05:37.390
Why?

05:38.310 --> 05:39.770
That's right, I...

05:40.980 --> 05:43.780
want to be a cougar, body and mind.

05:45.070 --> 05:46.780
Lick what you like.

05:47.150 --> 05:51.240
I'll break their spirit and leave them shaken!

05:51.240 --> 05:53.790
All right! Just run with that in mind.

05:54.750 --> 05:57.290
The biggest problem is you, Kotone.

05:58.540 --> 06:01.460
You're playing half heartedly the whole time.

06:01.460 --> 06:02.880
What are you doing?

06:02.880 --> 06:06.970
I'm not doing anything!

06:16.930 --> 06:21.480
I feel that you're perfectly capable
to play on par with Akadama.

06:21.480 --> 06:24.150
That's why I accepted.

06:25.480 --> 06:26.610
Is that so?

06:26.610 --> 06:27.780
Looks like it.

06:28.400 --> 06:32.780
Though, it depends on all of you using
your skills and strengths to their full extent.

06:33.200 --> 06:36.080
Your strength is instinct.

06:39.370 --> 06:43.420
Don't think, just use your instinct.

06:43.420 --> 06:45.500
Don't you want to win Wimbledon?

06:56.310 --> 06:59.140
I already know that.

06:59.520 --> 07:02.520
Why're you being so serious?!

07:04.150 --> 07:06.530
Hey, do you really get it?

07:06.530 --> 07:08.650
I get it!

07:09.820 --> 07:12.950
<i>This kind of romance-filled youth drama is irresistible!</i>

07:12.910 --> 07:14.660
<b></b>Quick reminder:

07:12.910 --> 07:14.660
<b></b>There's no Wimbledon in Soft Tennis!

07:16.910 --> 07:17.910
Work har—

07:17.910 --> 07:21.750
Victory! Victory! Akadama!

07:22.210 --> 07:23.750
Cheerleader?

07:30.760 --> 07:31.550
Yo.

07:31.550 --> 07:32.470
'Sup.

07:32.470 --> 07:33.970
An illusion?

07:38.100 --> 07:42.190
Shiradama Soft Tennis, fight!

07:42.190 --> 07:44.100
Go! Go! Asuna!

07:44.100 --> 07:46.110
Go! Go! Kotone!

07:46.110 --> 07:47.480
Go!

07:47.480 --> 07:50.150
Even a teacher is here, how amazing.

07:50.150 --> 07:50.990
Yeah.

07:52.490 --> 07:53.860
We can't lose.

07:57.700 --> 07:58.660
Sumino.

07:58.660 --> 08:02.120
Ah, the air pressure clearly rose.

08:02.120 --> 08:05.540
This aura... it's as from a wild beast.

08:12.090 --> 08:13.050
Sumino.

08:13.050 --> 08:13.930
Yeah.

08:13.930 --> 08:17.140
I've never seen such a sketchy aura.

08:18.890 --> 08:19.720
Here!

08:19.720 --> 08:23.350
<i>Asuna-san has... throughout the game,</i>

08:23.350 --> 08:26.060
<i>adapted to my serves.</i>

08:26.060 --> 08:30.480
<i>She isn't predicting the ball's path, but
simply running back and forth tirelessly.</i>

08:30.820 --> 08:31.320
That's all?

08:31.780 --> 08:34.450
<i>She has stronger legs than I could've ever imagined!</i>

08:34.450 --> 08:36.530
<i>But, if it's like this...</i>

08:36.530 --> 08:37.490
<i>Straight!</i>

08:38.160 --> 08:42.160
<i>I've given her the slip perfectly... It's
now in an area no back-guard can reach!</i>

08:43.790 --> 08:45.210
